title: $:/plugins/xiubo/research/readme

! Research customizations 1.0.0

This plugin supplies the research-specific presentation for the maintained Streams fork:

* Publication-aware breadcrumb labels, linked reference previews, and reference counts.
* Publication, author and topic templates, with Relink configuration for the associated list fields.
* Node marker colours, reference-panel spacing, editor font and background preferences.
* Streams in the main editor through the fork's supported integration.
* A small Recent sidebar template that excludes child nodes while retaining the core result-limit setting.

Streams owns node interaction and traversal. This plugin configures its extension points; it does not replace the Streams row, stylesheet, breadcrumb view or core editor body.

Personal helper macros, third-party plugin enable/disable choices, and other wiki preferences remain in the wiki.

!! Local migration

The project command `python3 bin/stage_research_upgrade.py --source-export SNAPSHOT.json --wiki-info tiddlywiki.info --target NEW_LOCAL_DIRECTORY` builds a fresh local copy. It checks the known customization bodies against `migrations/research_customizations.json` before making changes, archives the source, removes superseded overrides, and retires active template tags on documentation tiddlers while retaining their content and child notes.

Run `node bin/test_research_plugins.js PATH_TO_TIDDLYWIKI_RUNTIME` from the project to test the two plugins after startup. Keep the live wiki separate until the staged copy passes acceptance testing.

The Streams submodule pins commit `1a97a32` (Streams 1.3.1) from [[zhangxiubo/streams|https://github.com/zhangxiubo/streams]], branch `codex/research-streams`, based on upstream commit `17dfc9cf634338f986acc99413113884cfaba2a0`. The source change is also retained as `patches/streams/research-streams.patch`; it can be applied with `git am` to a checkout of that upstream commit.

!! Reproducible installation

Clone the project with `git clone --recurse-submodules --branch codex/tested-research-upgrade https://github.com/zhangxiubo/tiddlyresearch.git`. For an existing checkout, run `git submodule update --init --recursive`; the recursive option is needed for Moment's nested dependency. Use the recorded revisions, without `--remote`.

This checkout contains TiddlyWiki 5.4.1, Streams 1.3.1, Research customizations 1.0.0, Relink 2.6.1 / Relink Titles 2.6.0, Uglify 1.11.1, Moment 2.30.1, and Uni-link 3.0.4. Timeline 0.8.1, Edit-comptext 0.9.3, and the bundled HammerJS plugin retain the versions used in the local trial. Existing wiki plugin-disable preferences remain in the wiki.

Create a fresh research wiki with `node tiddlywiki.js PATH_TO_NEW_WIKI --init tiddlyresearch`. Start it with `node tiddlywiki.js PATH_TO_NEW_WIKI --listen host=127.0.0.1 port=8080`. Node.js runs this server; Python 3 is needed only for the customization migration and its tests. No npm installation is required to start the research edition.

The installation checks use Node.js 22. Run `node bin/test_research_plugins.js .`, `node bin/test_streams_graph.js`, `python3 bin/test_stage_research_upgrade.py`, and `node bin/test_research_installation.js`. The last command creates a temporary wiki, checks dependency versions, saves an edit over HTTP, restarts the server, and reloads the resulting HTML export. It listens only on a temporary localhost port and removes its test data afterwards.

The unmodified upstream core suite can also be run with `node tiddlywiki.js editions/test --test`. Its catalogue checks currently report ten metadata failures for missing names or stability declarations in the additional plugins, including retained HammerJS. These are separate from the passing research behavior tests; the full core suite is not reported as passing. Its five pending specifications are retained from upstream.

Run `python3 bin/test_stage_research_upgrade.py` to check migration behavior, and `node bin/verify_research_stage.js PATH_TO_TIDDLYWIKI_RUNTIME LOCAL_WIKI_DIRECTORY` to compare the staged wiki with its archived source. Verification allows local title/sidebar changes and the existing Today startup action's date refresh. It requires the original note bodies and relationships to remain unchanged.

Editing child nodes while a parent draft is open writes to the child nodes immediately. Discarding the parent draft discards the parent's draft text; it does not undo those separate child edits. Saved parent drafts merge structural updates through the Streams fork.

!! Relationship repair trial

Run `node bin/stage_stream_relationship_repair.js RUNTIME SOURCE_LOCAL_WIKI NEW_LOCAL_WIKI BACKUP_EXPORT.json` to create a separate trial with a review page and a reversible repair archive. The optional backup export supplies historical comparison evidence. The tool repairs only unique visible ownership one level below a stale parent pointer and removes references to absent child tiddlers. Ambiguous placement and shared references remain unchanged.

Run `node bin/stage_stream_relationship_repair.js RUNTIME --verify LOCAL_TRIAL_WIKI` to check source preservation, visible child ordering, repeatability, and the reverse import. Run `node bin/test_streams_graph.js` for the graph-repair tests.
